From 5462bdf47025859d2ae08ffab5f5e9714c4b9862 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Pfister <119864532+JJRPF@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 08:29:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] psci: CPU_ON, CPU_OFF and AFFINITY_INFO through the
 PSCI-via-EFI conduit

The kernel calls psci_efi_handler() as a plain function under its EFI
runtime map (Sven Peter's PSCI-via-EFI RFC, table layout as in the
kernel's struct efi_psci_table, num_features included).

CPU_ON dispatches a parked secondary to the kernel's entry point the
way smp_call4() does, without waiting. CPU_OFF cleans the core's L1,
posts the PMGR stop request and powers the core down with cpu_sleep()
as smp_stop_cpu() does; the next CPU_ON restarts it through the PMGR
start registers, it re-enters through RVBAR into the park loop and is
dispatched from there. AFFINITY_INFO reports OFF only once the core's
power status reads stopped.

The handler never prints (the UART is not mapped in the kernel's
context) and cleans or invalidates every spin-table access, since the
parked CPUs run with the MMU off.

kboot publishes the table, the image range and the MMIO the handler
touches in /chosen (aura,psci-*) for the EFI provider, only when the
payload DT has psci { method = "efi"; }. Built, not booted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AuzUDcEeRJQ6RCdWW2XWLb
